{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule0aB0V","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList.swift#L22","fileName":"AdjacencyList.swift"},"title":"AdjacencyList","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a weight can live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(amortized, like ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A hash table from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slot pair to position (open addressing with a multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/doc